commit 61315ebab1cf0e30e1834ffd6d83bab70601e356
Author: Francis Townsend-Merino <townsendmerino@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 09:24:14 2026 -0700
    MM1 MoE reserve (Francis's option A): an MoE placement's experts are reserved before its context grows
    
    SolvePlacement tries resident first, with every expert and its host copy
    reserved, then the expert cache with the top-k reserved; each picks its own
    context. More memory never gives a worse placement, MoE included, and Metal's
    context fit no longer falls back to the floor. The top-k reserve alone (the
    decision as worded) still fell from resident to expert-cached on a load whose
    experts are under one KV block, so the registered contingency was taken.
    
    Census: 3,534 of 29,637 groups change, 1,068 with a placement or class move,
    all upward and all MoE fixtures (listed in
    docs/measurements/mm1-moe-reserve-2026-10-27/). 84 of them are D4 (Metal's
    fit), which G-MA-1's rule as registered calls a failure; the golden is updated
    and the PR waits for Francis on that point. goinfer fit on CUDA now reports the
    real 26B and Qwen1.5-MoE as expert-cached instead of declined.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
